 "findings": [
  {
   "severity": "Info",
   "area": "part-number-lookup",
   "title": "Part-number search correctly redirects to the product page (verified — a strength)",
   "detail": "CONFIRMED on the live search box (2026-08-14): searching an exact Cat part number (e.g. 1R-1808) client-side redirects (Next.js RSC) straight to its product page /product/1R-1808 — the ideal known-item behavior. 10 part-number rows resolve this way. Note for the method: our raw server-side fetch is blind to client-side redirects and initially misread these as zero-result — the capture must detect the redirect (final URL), not read the empty pre-redirect grid."
  },
  {
   "severity": "High",
   "area": "use-case",
   "title": "Use-case queries return accessories, not the product",
   "detail": "1 job/use-case queries graded shallow (e.g. returning battery cables/covers for a battery query). Fix candidate: map task/use-case phrasing to product intent, not keyword tokens."
  },
  {
   "severity": "Critical",
   "area": "cross-reference",
   "title": "Competitor cross-reference searches return zero — ~$64M/yr coverage gap",
   "detail": "19 of 19 competitor part numbers (WIX, Baldwin, Fleetguard, Donaldson) returned 0 results in the top-25-by-demand sample, though Cat sells the exact equivalent (e.g. WIX 33626 → Cat 1R-0751; Baldwin B7299 → Cat 1R-1808). A shopper with the number off their old filter finds nothing — the highest-intent, highest-converting search on the site. Modeled loss, online-sales-anchored: ~$34M–$110M/yr recoverable (mid ~$64M). Fix candidate: index competitor interchange numbers as retrievable aliases."
  },
  {
   "severity": "Medium",
   "area": "compositional",
   "title": "Machine model is ignored in compositional queries",
   "detail": "2 model-qualified queries (e.g. \"oil filter for C15 engine\", \"bucket teeth for 336 excavator\") returned the right category but ignored the machine model, so results are not fitment-filtered. Fix candidate: parse and apply model/serial context."
  }
 ],
